  "step_3": "The information relevant to the decision reason—minimum probability per lottery—matches what the individual appears to consider: the probability of receiving a positive payoff (i.e., 'winning'). In both Lottery A and B, the smaller probability is associated with the higher monetary outcome (33% and 34%, respectively), which also corresponds to the chance of winning. Thus, the minimum probability aligns with the probability of winning in this context. The individual explicitly refers to a 1% increase in the chance to win, which corresponds to Lottery B having a 34% vs. 33% minimum probability. The justification ('höhere Wahrscheinlichkeit zu gewinnen') aligns with the rule of the decision reason, which prefers the lottery with the higher minimum probability. Therefore, the individual’s reasoning closely matches the application of the decision reason.",
  "final_assessment_score": 100
